Let me write the FB.

Need popcount. CODESYS has no built-in popcount; write loop.

Declaration: FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task with VAR_INPUT value DWORD; VAR_OUTPUT...; VAR prev : DWORD := 0; END_VAR

Implementation:

risingBits := value AND NOT prev;
fallingBits := prev AND NOT value;
hasChanged := value <> prev;
hasRisingEdges := risingBits <> 0;
hasFallingEdges := fallingBits <> 0;
count loops.
prev := value;

For NOT on DWORD, fine. Count: use FOR loop over 0..31 testing bits, or use USINT counter.

Let me write:

noOfRisingBits := 0;
FOR i := 0 TO 31 DO
  IF (risingBits AND SHL(DWORD#1, i)) <> 0 THEN
    noOfRisingBits := noOfRisingBits + 1;
  END_IF
END_FOR

i : INT. Actually use DWORD shift. Simpler: tempWord := risingBits; FOR i:=0 TO 31 DO IF (tempWord AND 1)<>0 THEN... tempWord := SHR(tempWord,1);

Use INT i, DWORD tmp.

Note: hasChanged uses value<>prev which is equivalent to masks nonzero, correct.

Write implementation carefully.

